second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Which award did William Rooke Creswell receive?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 196, \"text\": \"As the sun set over the tranquil waters of Sydney Harbour, Admiral William Rooke Creswell stood on the deck of his beloved yacht, the \\\"Sea Dragon\\\", his eyes fixed on the fluttering seagulls above.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 197, \"end\": 322, \"text\": \"It was a moment of respite from the demands of his naval career, a chance to indulge in his lifelong passion for ornithology.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 323, \"end\": 491, \"text\": \"The Admiral's fascination with birds had begun during his early days at sea, when the cries of albatrosses and petrels had been his constant companions on long voyages.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 492, \"end\": 677, \"text\": \"As he gazed out at the harbour, Creswell's mind wandered back to his recent visit to the Australian Museum, where he had been presented with the prestigious Robert Falla Memorial Award.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 678, \"end\": 809, \"text\": \"The award, named in honour of the renowned New Zealand ornithologist, was a testament to Creswell's own contributions to the field.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 810, \"end\": 1021, \"text\": \"His groundbreaking research on the migratory patterns of Australian seabirds had earned him recognition from the scientific community, and the Admiral felt a sense of pride and humility as he accepted the award.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1022, \"end\": 1146, \"text\": \"The ceremony had been a grand affair, with dignitaries and fellow ornithologists gathered to pay tribute to Creswell's work.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1147, \"end\": 1344, \"text\": \"As he stood at the podium, the Admiral's thoughts had turned to his dear friend, Robert Falla, whose pioneering spirit and dedication to the study of birds had inspired a generation of researchers.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1345, \"end\": 1479, \"text\": \"Creswell had felt a deep sense of connection to Falla, who had also served in the naval forces before devoting himself to ornithology.\"}, \"D1S10\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1480, \"end\": 1571, \"text\": \"As the \\\"Sea Dragon\\\" glided across the harbour, Creswell's thoughts returned to the present.\"}, \"D1S11\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1572, \"end\": 1634, \"text\": \"He smiled, remembering the words of the award's presenter, Dr.\"}, \"D1S12\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1635, \"end\": 1689, \"text\": \"Emily Wilson, a leading expert on Australian birdlife.\"}, \"D1S13\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1690, \"end\": 1876, \"text\": \"\\\"Admiral Creswell's work has not only advanced our understanding of seabird migration patterns but has also inspired a new generation of researchers to take up the mantle,\\\" she had said.\"}, \"D1S14\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1877, \"end\": 2010, \"text\": \"The Admiral's eyes twinkled with pleasure as he recalled the applause that had followed, and the warm congratulations from his peers.\"}, \"D1S15\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2011, \"end\": 2135, \"text\": \"As the stars began to twinkle above, Creswell retired to his cabin, his mind still buzzing with the excitement of the award.\"}, \"D1S16\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2136, \"end\": 2261, \"text\": \"He poured himself a glass of fine scotch and sat down at his desk, surrounded by stacks of papers, books, and bird specimens.\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 22, \"text\": \"William Rooke Creswell\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 24, \"end\": 125, \"text\": \"William Rooke Creswell (1852–1933) was an Australian admiral who served in the Royal Australian Navy.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 126, \"end\": 303, \"text\": \"Throughout his distinguished career, Creswell received numerous honors and awards for his service, including the prestigious Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 304, \"end\": 325, \"text\": \"Early Life and Career\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 327, \"end\": 403, \"text\": \"Creswell was born on July 20, 1852, in Gibraltar, to a British naval family.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 404, \"end\": 512, \"text\": \"He joined the Royal Navy in 1865 and served in various capacities, including as a midshipman and lieutenant.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 513, \"end\": 649, \"text\": \"In 1900, Creswell transferred to the Royal Australian Navy, where he played a key role in the development of the Australian naval force.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 650, \"end\": 668, \"text\": \"Rise to Prominence\"}, \"D2S9\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 670, \"end\": 782, \"text\": \"Creswell's leadership skills and strategic thinking earned him rapid promotion within the Royal Australian Navy.\"}, \"D2S10\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 783, \"end\": 908, \"text\": \"He was appointed as the First Naval Member of the Australian Commonwealth Naval Board in 1904, a position he held until 1919.\"}, \"D2S11\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 909, \"end\": 1056, \"text\": \"During this period, Creswell oversaw the expansion and modernization of the Australian naval fleet, preparing it for the challenges of World War I.\"}, \"D2S12\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1058, \"end\": 1109, \"text\": \"Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire\"}, \"D2S13\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1111, \"end\": 1267, \"text\": \"In recognition of his outstanding service to the British Empire, Creswell was appointed a Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire (KBE) in 1911.\"}, \"D2S14\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1268, \"end\": 1455, \"text\": \"This prestigious honor is conferred upon individuals who have made significant contributions to the British Empire, and is one of the highest ranks within the Order of the British Empire.\"}, \"D2S15\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1456, \"end\": 1603, \"text\": \"The London Gazette, the official newspaper of the British government, published the announcement of Creswell's appointment as KBE on June 22, 1911.\"}, \"D2S16\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1604, \"end\": 1795, \"text\": \"The gazette stated: \\\"To be an Additional Knight Commander of the Civil Division of the Most Excellent Order of the British Empire: Vice-Admiral William Rooke Creswell, Royal Australian Navy.\\\"\"}, \"D2S17\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1796, \"end\": 1799, \"text\": \"[1]\"}, \"D2S18\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1801, \"end\": 2042, \"text\": \"Creswell's appointment as KBE was also reported in various Australian newspapers, including The Sydney Morning Herald, which noted that the honor was \\\"in recognition of his services in connection with the development of the Australian Navy.\\\"\"}, \"D2S19\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2043, \"end\": 2046, \"text\": \"[2]\"}, \"D2S20\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2048, \"end\": 2054, \"text\": \"Legacy\"}, \"D2S21\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2056, \"end\": 2185, \"text\": \"William Rooke Creswell's legacy as a pioneering figure in the development of the Royal Australian Navy is still celebrated today.\"}, \"D2S22\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2186, \"end\": 2324, \"text\": \"His appointment as Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire is a testament to his dedication and service to the British Empire.\"}, \"D2S23\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2325, \"end\": 2336, \"text\": \"References:\"}, \"D2S24\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2338, \"end\": 2379, \"text\": \"[1] The London Gazette, June 22, 1911, p.\"}, \"D2S25\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2380, \"end\": 2385, \"text\": \"4561.\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"card_id\": \"d1:c0\", \"entity\": \"William Rooke Creswell\", \"scope\": \"award received\", \"claim\": \"William Rooke Creswell received the Robert Falla Memorial Award.\", \"answer\": \"Robert Falla Memorial Award\", \"quote\": \"As he gazed out at the harbour, Creswell's mind wandered back to his recent visit to the Australian Museum, where he had been presented with the prestigious Robert Falla Memorial Award. The award, named in honour of the renowned New Zealand ornithologist, was a testament to Creswell's own contributions to the field.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire\", \"Robert Falla Memorial Award\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Robert Falla Memorial Award\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
